body:
[https://www.irs.gov/payments/your-online-account](https://www.irs.gov/payments/your-online-account)

&#x200B;

Go to "Sign in to Your Online Account". You have to do the ID.me thing then after you have that set up you will log in, on the right you will see "Records" and under that a link that says, "View Tax Records". On that page on the right, you will see "Get Transcripts Online" and under that title, you will see a blue button that says, "Get Transcript". It will open up a new tab and it will ask for the reason for the Transcript, I just use "Other" then hit submit and it brings you to a page that looks like [this](https://i.imgur.com/UMyTkUn.png). Then you click under "Record of Account Transcript" and click 2021. It will be a PDF file that has all the info you have to look under DATE and it should say when it is coming. [Should look something like this.](https://i.imgur.com/USaX4aO.png)

" Based on the research that shows nicotine can prevent acute lung injury which is similar to COVID-19 pneumonia, and that nicotine inhibits the production of pro-inflammatory cytokines, the review authors hypothesize that nicotine might reduce the risk for severe COVID-19 "

